Https://talesprintindia-cyber.github.io/javenyx/ Check what is the problem

Here are the most likely reasons why [https://talesprintindia-cyber.github.io/javenyx/](https://talesprintindia-cyber.github.io/javenyx/) might show an error (such as a 404 Not Found or a blank page), along with how to fix them:

1. GitHub Pages is Not Enabled on the Repository

The Problem: Simply creating a repository named javenyx under talesprintindia-cyber does not automatically publish it to the web.

The Fix:

Go to your GitHub repository: [https://github.com/talesprintindia-cyber/javenyx](https://github.com/talesprintindia-cyber/javenyx)

Click on Settings (gear icon on the top tab bar).

In the left sidebar, click on Pages.

Under Build and deployment > Source, ensure Deploy from a branch is selected.

Under Branch, select main (or master) and set the folder to / (root).

Click Save. (Wait 2–3 minutes for the build process to complete).

2. Incorrect File Naming or Missing index.html

The Problem: GitHub Pages specifically looks for a file named index.html in the root folder to serve as your homepage. If your main landing file is named Index.html (capital I), home.html, or saved accidentally as index.html.txt, the URL will throw a 404 Not Found error.

The Fix:

Open your repository on GitHub.

Verify that index.html is present at the top level (root directory) and typed in all lowercase.

Ensure you have also uploaded category.html, cart.html, cart.js, products.json, and your logo images to the exact same root directory.

3. Mixed Up Repository Name vs. Account Username

The Problem: Your GitHub account username is talesprintindia-cyber. Make sure the repository name matches what you typed in your browser.

The Fix:

If the repository name is javenyx, the correct URL is [https://talesprintindia-cyber.github.io/javenyx/](https://talesprintindia-cyber.github.io/javenyx/).

If the repository is named something else (e.g., javenyx-store), update your URL accordingly.

4. Browser Caching Old Builds

The Problem: Sometimes GitHub Pages takes 2 to 5 minutes to deploy after a fresh commit, or your browser caches a previous 404 state.

The Fix: Open the link in an Incognito / Private Browsing window or press Ctrl + Shift + R (Cmd + Shift + R on Mac) to hard-refresh the page.

